            <ArticleTitle>Failure of daptomycin β-Lactam combination therapy to prevent resistance emergence in Enterococcus faecium.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0732-8893(17)30341-3</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.diagmicrobio.2017.10.017</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Daptomycin β-Lactam combination therapy offers &quot;protection&quot; against daptomycin non-susceptibility (DNS) development in Enterococcus faecium. We report failure of this strategy and the importance of source control. Mutations were detected in the LiaF and cls genes in DNS isolates. A single DNS isolate contained an unrecognized mutation, which requires confirmation.</AbstractText>
